<title>SWITZERLAND: Immuno bearers inch up on Baxter deal.</title>
<headline>Immuno bearers inch up on Baxter deal.</headline>
<dateline>ZURICH 1996-08-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Immuno International AG's bearer shares rose slightly on news Baxter International Inc planned to acquire the blood-products and vaccines company in a deal worth around 850 million Swiss francs.</p>
<p>Bearers were bid at 885 francs in early trade, off a high of 889 but above the close at 883, in brisk business.</p>
<p>The companies said Baxter planned to offer 900 francs per bearer share in a tender to be launched within three years.</p>
<p>&quot;With yesterday's price of 883 francs, this was not especially generous,&quot; one dealer said, adding expectations for a big rise could fade if a rival offer does not emerge.</p>
<p>-- Zurich newsroom +41 1 631 7340</p>
</text>
